  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only configuration (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) achieves 0.650 accuracy. Adding ResNet50 image features via concat fusion (config_030) slightly degrades performance to 0.632, suggesting the image channel introduces noise or that concat is too aggressive a combination strategy. Uncertainty: It is unclear whether the ~2-point degradation is an artifact of the naive concat fusion (which equally weights all features) or a fundamental lack of complementary signal in ResNet50 image features. This experiment (config_031) tests weighted fusion as the sole change relative to config_030, isolating the fusion strategy effect while keeping the proven scvi_n200/multiprofile/avgpool backbone and ResNet50 encoder constant. If weighted fusion recovers or exceeds 0.650, it indicates the image carries complementary signal that requires learned gating; if it also fails to beat the RNA-only baseline, it strongly suggests ResNet50 features are uninformative for this task regardless of fusion, directing future budget toward either a stronger image encoder (ViT-L) or confirming RNA-only as the optimal architecture. This is the cleanest, most interpretable single-variable follow-up and the highest-information next step under a limited budget."
}

